{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Lotan's sister Timna.</b> Like \"and Tubal-cain's sister Naamah\" (Genesis 4:22), \"and their sisters Zeruiah and Abigail\" (I Chronicles 2:16), \"and Tamar their sister\" (ibid. 3:9), \"and Serah their sister\" (Genesis 46:17), for the practice is to trace the daughter's lineage to the brothers. Now it would have been fitting to list Timna above together with the sons of Seir — Dishon, Ezer, Dishan — and Timna their sister, but she was Lotan's sister, daughter of his father and daughter of his mother, not the sister of the other brothers. Therefore Scripture wished to trace her lineage to him. Or perhaps she was his sister from the mother's side and not from the father's side, and she is not a daughter of Seir the Horite."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:28.920301021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}